{"query":"October 2020 state mail ballot receipt deadlines postmarked by Election Day NCSL","results":[{"date":"Jun 29, 2026","position":1,"site_name":"www.ncsl.org","snippet":"The table below shows which states require mailed ballots to be received by Election Day or postmarked by Election Day and provides deadline details for each state.","title":"Table 11: Receipt and Postmark Deadlines for Absentee/Mail ...","url":"https://www.ncsl.org/elections-and-campaigns/table-11-receipt-and-postmark-deadlines-for-absentee-mail-ballots"},{"date":"Oct 29, 2020","position":2,"site_name":"www.ncsbe.gov","snippet":"County boards of elections in North Carolina will accept mail-in ballots received by November 12, as long as they are postmarked by Election Day, November 3. The U.S. Supreme Court ruled Wednesday to uphold this deadline.","title":"Receipt Deadline is November 12 for Ballots Postmarked by ...","url":"https://www.ncsbe.gov/news/press-releases/2020/10/29/receipt-deadline-november-12-ballots-postmarked-election-day"},{"position":3,"site_name":"ballotpedia.org","snippet":"How to use this interactive table: The table comprises five columns: 1. State 2. In-person request deadline (the last day voters can submit absentee/mail-in voting requests in person, if applicable) 3. Online request deadline (the last day voters can submit absentee/mail-in voting requests online, if applicable) 4. Mail request deadline (the last d...","title":"Absentee/mail-in voting deadlines, 2020 - Ballotpedia","url":"https://ballotpedia.org/Absentee/mail-in_voting_deadlines,_2020"},{"position":4,"site_name":"www.cisa.gov","snippet":"This data is sourced from state election calendars, NCSL, NASS, and NASED. CISA does not provide any warranties of any kind regarding this information. Voters should seek the most up-to-date election information from their state and local elected oficials.","title":"Mail-In Voting Processing Factors - CISA","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/publications/mail-in-voting-processing-factors_oct-8_508.pdf"},{"position":5,"site_name":"ballotpedia.org","snippet":"States have different deadlines for when absentee/mail-in ballots must be received in order to be counted. In some states, these deadlines can also vary based on whether the ballot is returned by mail or in person, and whether the voter is a member of the United States military or living overseas.","title":"Absentee/mail-in ballot receipt deadlines by state","url":"https://ballotpedia.org/Absentee/mail-in_ballot_receipt_deadlines_by_state"},{"date":"Oct 27, 2020","position":6,"site_name":"edition.cnn.com","snippet":"An interactive, national overview of which states allow mail-in voting, when ballots need to arrive to be counted, and where Americans can vote early in person.","title":"Mail-in ballots: When every state starts counting","url":"https://edition.cnn.com/interactive/2020/politics/mail-in-voting/"},{"date":"Nov 3, 2020","position":7,"site_name":"www.nbcnews.com","snippet":"Most states require that ballots be postmarked and received by Nov. 3, but some require that they be postmarked by the day before and received within six days, while others require a...","title":"Map: The states that accept mailed ballots after Election Day","url":"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2020-election/map-states-accept-mailed-ballots-after-election-day-n1246044"}],"total_results":7,"page":0}